<title>USA: Wisconsin Central Q1 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Wisconsin Central Q1 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>ROSEMONT, Ill. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>WISCONSIN CENTRAL TRANSPORTATION CORPORATION</p>
<p>						     1997	     1996</p>
<p>Quarter ending March 31:</p>
<p> Operating revenues (1)	     $80,261,000     $65,365,000</p>
<p> Operating expenses		    65,176,000	60,613,000</p>
<p> Income from operations(1)	   15,085,000	 4,752,000</p>
<p>Income before equity in net-</p>
<p>  income of affiliates		  7,361,000	 1,994,000</p>
<p>Equity in net income of TRanz Rail</p>
<p>						3,170,000	 2,913,000</p>
<p> Equity in net income of EWS	  7,103,000	 3,159,000</p>
<p> Equity in net income affiliates   10,273,000	 6,072,000</p>
<p> Net income				17,634,000	 8,066,000</p>
<p> Average shrs outstanding	    50,803,000	50,521,000</p>
<p> Earnings per common share outstanding   0.35		0.16</p>
<p>(1) Certain amounts which were previously classified as non-operating have been reclassified as operating revenues. The amounts reclassified were $1,465,000 and $337,000 for the quarter ended March 31, 1997 and March 31, 1996, respectively.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
